{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03382",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.55,
      "end_seconds": 4.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.43,
      "end_seconds": 9.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 11.58,
      "end_seconds": 19.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.85,
      "text": "Um, you know, morning, doctor. I'll stay and fill in anything that's missed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.1,
      "end_seconds": 25.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "So, yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 26.52,
      "end_seconds": 29.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "She's been having cloudy smelly urine, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.55,
      "end_seconds": 36.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "When did this begin? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.86,
      "end_seconds": 42.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Let me think, you know, for two days, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.77,
      "end_seconds": 46.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.16,
      "end_seconds": 53.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "Pain in the lower tummy goes along with it, most of the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.76,
      "end_seconds": 57.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Have you had confusion?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.06,
      "end_seconds": 82.89,
      "duration_seconds": 24.83,
      "text": "Yeah, that too. And fever and shivers as well, since Monday. Right, uh, with fever and shivers, it feels moderate to me. As for pain in the lower tummy, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.64,
      "end_seconds": 86.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.05,
      "end_seconds": 91.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "It's on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.95,
      "end_seconds": 98.97,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "Have you had cloudy smelly urine before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.52,
      "end_seconds": 106.58,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened last year, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.37,
      "end_seconds": 125.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "So, any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.82,
      "end_seconds": 140.76,
      "duration_seconds": 10.94,
      "text": "I've had acid reflux for two years now. Gout, for about ten years. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.49,
      "end_seconds": 149.33,
      "duration_seconds": 7.84,
      "text": "So, yes, gout is known to us, good to have that clear. Are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.36,
      "end_seconds": 155.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.03,
      "end_seconds": 158.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.69,
      "end_seconds": 163.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.16,
      "end_seconds": 177.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.3,
      "end_seconds": 185.41,
      "duration_seconds": 7.11,
      "text": "It's omeprazole, 20 milligrams, maybe, once a day for the reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.2,
      "end_seconds": 192.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.71,
      "end_seconds": 203.01,
      "duration_seconds": 10.3,
      "text": "Okay, so not with me. I'll bring it next time. Uh, I'm on febuxostat, 80 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.37,
      "end_seconds": 207.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Since when have you been taking it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.48,
      "end_seconds": 215.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.01,
      "text": "Nearly five years now. I'm on a urinary catheter, in place."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.55,
      "end_seconds": 218.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.97,
      "end_seconds": 224.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Just part of my thyroid removed, years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.83,
      "end_seconds": 230.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.56,
      "end_seconds": 235.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Yes, walnuts, it gives me hives."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.03,
      "end_seconds": 240.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "How about back pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.37,
      "end_seconds": 243.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "No back pain, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.88,
      "end_seconds": 247.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Have you noticed cough, vomiting or fall?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.51,
      "end_seconds": 254.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "No cough, vomiting or fall, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.6,
      "end_seconds": 258.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.38,
      "end_seconds": 263.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "No, uh, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.81,
      "end_seconds": 268.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.07,
      "end_seconds": 278.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.16,
      "end_seconds": 300.4,
      "duration_seconds": 8.24,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 93, BP is 122 over 74, temperature 39.0, saturation 97 percent, respiratory rate 21."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.13,
      "end_seconds": 303.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.94,
      "end_seconds": 309.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "I'll explain what these mean in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.28,
      "end_seconds": 313.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.87,
      "end_seconds": 317.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.66,
      "end_seconds": 337.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "The catheter bag has cloudy urine and there is tenderness above the pubic bone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.3,
      "end_seconds": 346.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Okay, that's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.23,
      "end_seconds": 362.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, I'd lean towards a catheter-related urinary infection. I can't rule out urosepsis yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 364.49,
      "end_seconds": 366.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.65,
      "end_seconds": 386.31,
      "duration_seconds": 17.66,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a catheter-related urinary infection do well once it's treated properly. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've had cloudy smelly urine for two days, and no back pain or cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 386.83,
      "end_seconds": 390.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "That's what happened, um, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.72,
      "end_seconds": 397.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "I'm going to order a urine culture, for possible urinary infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 398.11,
      "end_seconds": 401.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Right, when would that take place?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 403.62,
      "end_seconds": 431.54,
      "duration_seconds": 27.92,
      "text": "I'm going to order blood tests, for fever. The treatment will be co-amoxiclav, 625 milligrams, three times a day, seven days. You take it by mouth. That should help with catheter urinary infection. Change the catheter and drink plenty. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 433.28,
      "end_seconds": 435.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Okay, makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 437.02,
      "end_seconds": 444.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "I'll want another look in two days. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 446.21,
      "end_seconds": 449.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 451.51,
      "end_seconds": 452.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}